Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Observers", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An observer is a saturated chain, its positions the ticks of a clock. Two \
observers exchange light: the message relation sends a tick of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1606b47d-795a-4739-8a40-2360c84b7a0b"],
 " to the ticks of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["b", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c537942d-71b7-4a43-85e9-7af3715a39bc"],
 " it reaches by a light ray, and the echo relation returns the message to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c970aefa-f38f-427d-8daa-2c76c5ba25cc"],
 ". A single-valued selection of the relation that preserves the tick order \
is a message function in the sense of Ehlers, Pirani and Schild (axiom D1); \
an echo function is the composition of a message function to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["b", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d3446c0-0d26-4cc8-bb7e-1cd3c175d595"],
 " with a message function back to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73b64914-3d29-4f3a-8c17-573a53eb959b"],
 ". The message and echo heads are read for their relation, their graph and \
the number of such functions. The radar chart of an observer assigns to every \
event in its radar domain the emission tick ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7371e650-7b29-4bfe-af80-b837cbeb4d43"],
 " of the latest tick that can signal the event and the reception tick ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "672219d4-f27f-4c32-9a37-a211e12b6eba"],
 " of the earliest tick the event can signal, hence the radar time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c85d09d-e498-44e9-b502-8c038c4945a1"],
 " and the radar distance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50a50ce1-8dfd-4e2d-a5b7-51e6910e65c2"],
 "; the distance is unsigned, so a single observer in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7d06eea-1b48-43c0-ae65-6c84c3931bb7"],
 " dimensions sees the two sides of its worldline folded onto each other."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

